    "title": "See which Lower Hudson Valley Shoprite stores are open Easter Sunday",
    "text": "April 3, 2026, 10:57 a.m. ETEaster weekend is here, are you cooking up a feast to celebrate? If you've forgotten eggs for dying or ham for dinner, worry not— many ShopRite locations across the Lower Hudson Valley are open all weekend, including on Easter Sunday.Read on for hours and locations. Looking for a different supermarket chain's hours for Easter? Check out this story.ShopRite hours for Easter SundayShopRite has numerous stores in the region, hours can vary by location and a couple will be closed. Here are the hours:ShopRite of Tuckahoe, in Yonkers, will be open 7 a.m. to 7 p.m.ShopRite of Greenway Plaza, in Yonkers, will be open 7 a.m. to 7 p.m.West Nyack will be closedWhite Plains will be open 7 a.m. to 5 p.m.Thornwood will be open 6 a.m. to 5 p.m.Scarsdale will be open 7 a.m. to 5 p.m.ShopRite of Pelham Parkway will be open 7 a.m. to 6 p.m.Pearl River will be open 6 a.m. to 6 p.m.New Rochelle will be open 7 a.m. to 5 p.m.New City will be closed.ShopRite of Elmsford-Greenburgh will be open 7 a.m. to 5 p.m.Carmel will be open 7 a.m. to 5 p.m.Croton-on-Hudson will be open 7 a.m. to 5 p.m.Mount Kisco will be open 7 a.m. to 5 p.m.",
